  "comments": {
    "PNGX-417": [
      {
        "author": {
          "handle": "mia",
          "id": "user-mia",
          "name": "Mia Schultz"
        },
        "body": "Support has 3 customers reporting that documents uploaded after ~02:10 don't show up in search. Re-uploading doesn't help.",
        "created_at": "2026-06-06T03:05:00Z",
        "id": "comment-pngx-417-1",
        "issue": "PNGX-417",
        "updated_at": "2026-06-06T03:05:00Z"
      },
      {
        "author": {
          "handle": "dana",
          "id": "user-dana",
          "name": "Dana Okafor"
        },
        "body": "Indexer throughput flatlined at 02:08, right after a bulk batch raised during commit. Bouncing paperless-worker unblocks it for a few minutes, then it wedges again the next time a batch errors. Logs are full of `LockBusy: failed to acquire index writer lock`.",
        "created_at": "2026-06-06T03:40:00Z",
        "id": "comment-pngx-417-2",
        "issue": "PNGX-417",
        "updated_at": "2026-06-06T03:40:00Z"
      },
      {
        "author": {
          "handle": "ravi",
          "id": "user-ravi",
          "name": "Ravi Menon"
        },
        "body": "This is the index writer lock not being released once a batch hits an error mid-commit \u2014 a reindex clears it. I'm chasing the exact code path in #paperless-oncall; will link the fix here once we land it. Not a Redis/heap issue.",
        "created_at": "2026-06-06T04:15:00Z",
        "id": "comment-pngx-417-3",
        "issue": "PNGX-417",
        "updated_at": "2026-06-06T04:15:00Z"
      }
    ]
  },
